  "description": "WUZTUI crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C48 H68 Dy4 N4 O25 2+,2(Cl1 1-),4(C1 H4 O1),8(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.576-4.994 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.38-166.52°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4(μ4-OH)(HL)(H2L)3(H2O)4]Cl2·(CH3OH)4·(H2O)8. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
